  "result": "I would rewire the human nervous system so that realizing you are wrong feels like relief instead of threat.\n\nRight now, having a deeply held belief challenged triggers the same defensive circuitry as a physical attack\u2014ego protection, doubling down, closing ranks. Because of that, an enormous share of human intelligence isn't spent solving problems; it's spent defending narratives, saving face, and attacking whoever threatens our certainty. \n\nIf updating your mind felt genuinely good\u2014the way stepping out of tight shoes or solving a puzzle feels\u2014propaganda, dogma, and performative outrage would lose most of their fuel. People would still have conflicting values and hard problems to solve, but disagreements would actually move forward instead of calcifying into trenches. Civilizations wouldn't have to hit a wall just to admit an old idea stopped working.",
